+///
+/// A chunked message is as long as its first chunk declares, up to 4 GiB, and its chunks are held until the last one
+/// arrives: nothing but this bounds what a peer can make the receiver hold. Channels whose messages can legitimately
+/// be longer (clipboard data) declare their own maximum, and so can channels whose protocol bounds them well below.
+pub const DEFAULT_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE: usize = 64 * 1024 * 1024;
